    "comment": "Class (B) saturates mod-3 with NO per-step LDP cost: g only touches a_n, contributing an O(1) factor to the log-partition, an O(1/n) correction to the LDP exponent. But this is essentially tautological: g couples to R_n by design, so OF COURSE it can fix the mod-3 marginal. The honest question is mod 3^k for k > 1, requiring g to couple to the last k valuations -- equivalent to conditioning on R_n mod 3^k itself.  See classB_mod9 below for the next test."
  },
